      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1291",
      ":question/problem": "The points $A$, $B$, and $C$ form a triangle. The points $B$ and $C$ are $24m$ apart. If the measure of the angle at the point $A$ is $108^{\u2218}$ and the measure of the angle at the point $B$ is $33^{\u2218}$, how far is point $A$ from point $C$? Round the answer to the nearest tenth.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
